Lab: Password reset broken logic

Goal:-      This lab's password reset functionality is vulnerable. To solve the lab, reset Carlos's password then log in and access his "My account" page.
            Your credentials: wiener:peter
            Victim's username: carlos

Observation:- #The password reset functionality allows changing a password only based on the username parameter.
              #The application does not validate that the request belongs to the authenticated user.
              #There is no reset token or verification mechanism tied to the specific user.
              #Because of this, the attacker can intercept the request and modify the username to another user (Carlos).

Steps to solve :- 
        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Go to Login page  
        Step3:- try forget password using the credential of wiener and capture the request in the burpsuit
        step4:- change the name from wiener to carlos in burp repeter 
        Step5:- send reqest
        Step6:- password changed 
        Step7:-login in my-account

Root Cause:- #The server trusts user supplied input (username parameter) in the password reset request.
             #The application fails to enforce proper authorization checks.
             #The reset process does not use a secure password reset token tied to the user session.
             #As a result, an attacker can change another user's password by manipulating request parameters.
Vulnerability Type:- #Broken Authentication
